- op: discuss  # 87c1
  at: '2026-11-17T07:40:17Z'  # 87c1
  by: agent  # 87c1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 87c1
  clock: 4  # 87c1
  nonce: 87c1  # 87c1
  message: "Fixed in PR #2219 (dev 26f51346b). Root cause as filed: the nudge needed the virtualenv and a 41 s forge call inside a 5 s hook, and printed nothing when either failed. Now it reads the verdict each scheduled run publishes to origin/badges with local git commands after one fetch bounded at 1.5 s, shares a 3.6 s budget between that fetch and the tracker call, and prints a line when it cannot determine the status. EVIDENCE, re-run on merged dev 2026-11-17 07:45 UTC, the item's own repro form: `echo '{}' | env -i HOME=$HOME PATH=/usr/bin:/bin bash .agent/hooks/claude-code/session-start.sh` -> exit 0 in 0.60 s, and the output holds 'ALSO (separate item): Scheduled-run status not checked: no verdict file under scheduled/ on origin/badges. Run `./scripts/ci-debug cron-status`.' (before the fix the same environment printed nothing about the scheduled run; the latest full-suite verdict, pipeline 6480, is red and no verdict is published yet, so 'not checked' is the correct arm). The RED arm is shown by tests/test_cron_status_nudge.py, which runs the script under env -i against a repository whose origin/badges holds a failed verdict. NOT ASSERTED HERE: the RED line against a verdict published by a real scheduled run; that waits for the first run after the merge and is tracked on WI-jomid. Known gap, not fixed: a nightly leg that never publishes is not reported."  # 87c1
